config APEX_RADIO_THREAD_PRIORITY
    int "Radio transaction thread priority"
    range 0 14
    default 0
    help
      Preemptible Zephyr priority for authenticated packet processing. Lower
      values run first. USB interrupts and cooperative workqueues still take
      precedence. The thread blocks while transmitting or waiting for traffic.

config APEX_RADIO_BENCHMARK
    bool "Enable the bounded radio delivery benchmark"
    default n
    depends on APEX_G4B_RADIO_INPUT && SHELL
    help
      Add apex radio_bench to send 1000 empty keyboard reports through the
      normal radio and receiver USB path. Requires direct USB output and
      stops after ten seconds or an endpoint/session change. Development only.

config APEX_RADIO_KEYBOARD_EVENT_RX
    bool "Wake the keyboard radio thread on packet reception"
    default n
    depends on APEX_G4B_RADIO_INPUT && APEX_RADIO_HOPPING
    help
      Route RADIO DISABLED through PPI channel 19 to EGU3. This uses
      SWI3/EGU3 instead of replacing Bluetooth's direct RADIO interrupt.
      Enabled only after Bluetooth shutdown; incompatible with another EGU3
      or nrfx software-interrupt user.

config APEX_RADIO_TEST_CHANNEL
    int "Fixed radio test channel (MHz above 2400)"
    range 0 80
    default 40
    help
      Both devices must use the same value. This selects a single frequency
      for development measurements; it does not enable channel hopping.

config APEX_RADIO_HOPPING
    bool "Experimental timed channel hopping"
    default n
    depends on APEX_G4B_RADIO_INPUT || APEX_RECEIVER_RADIO_INPUT
    help
      Negotiate a session-bound channel map and hop in 20 ms slots. Owns
      TIMER2 and PPI channels 17, 18 and 19 after Bluetooth has shut down.
      Requires matching keyboard and receiver builds. Not a 1 kHz scheduler.
